Package: passerelle-host
Architecture: all
Depends: python3,
         ${python3:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: cmake,
            qemu-system-x86
Description: host tools for the Passerelle 9P2000.L / virtiofs stack
 Passerelle is a 9P2000.L and virtiofs client for QNX 8.0 guests under
 QEMU. This package ships the host side of the project: the Python tools
 that prepare and drive a shared filesystem for the guest.
 .
 Console tools installed:
  * qshare  - generate the QEMU options that export a host directory;
  * qrun    - start a QEMU guest with a share and wait for its agent;
  * fsproof - replay a recorded 9P trace against the client stack;
  * pbench  - the pass/fail benchmark harness of the specification.
 .
 The QNX SDP is not part of this package: it is licensed and not
 redistributable. Building the guest driver needs cmake and a C11
 compiler (see Recommends); the host tools themselves are pure Python.
